GameNetworkingSockets TURN lifetime patch.

Upstream: https://github.com/ValveSoftware/GameNetworkingSockets tag v1.6.0,
commit 2cb93a06350bb065db53abdb0d87cf297e0bfd34. Apply in that checkout with
"git apply <this file>" (or "patch -p1 < <this file>"), then build and install
into a new prefix; docs/turn-relay.md has the commands.

The native ICE client keeps a relayed connection alive for its whole life:
- TURN permissions go out again every 240 s of their 300 s lifetime (RFC 5766
  section 8); before, the only CreatePermission lapsed and the relay dropped
  the peer after 5 minutes.
- Refresh, CreatePermission and Allocate answers are checked: a stale nonce
  (438, or 401 with a new nonce) is resent with the new nonce; 437 or an
  allocation past its lifetime is torn down and allocated again; any other
  refusal is reported and retried before the allocation lapses. Before, an
  error answer to Refresh counted as success and ended the refreshes.
- P2P_TURN_ServerList/UserList/PassList set on a live connection reach its
  ICE session: every allocation from then on uses the new login, a relay that
  failed is tried again, and a live allocation keeps the username that
  created it (another one is refused with 441, RFC 5766 section 4).
- steamnetworkingtypes.h defines STEAMNETWORKINGSOCKETS_TURN_LIFETIME.

